    "concept": {
      "variant_id": "B1-v001",
      "brief_id": "B1",
      "direction": "soft_pebble",
      "name": "Pebble Slab 110",
      "form_language": "A flattened pebble: plan view is a soft lozenge with continuous large-radius corners, elevation is a low slab with a gentle crown on top and a matching belly, the parting line sits low as a single straight shadow gap that reads as intent rather than a seam. The front face is a calm field: one small dark display window set left of centre, a low-slot intake grille running along the lower third, and nothing else. No bezels, no inserts, no trim; the whole character comes from the radius rhythm and one uniform light texture.",
      "silhouette": "pebble",
      "envelope_mm": {
        "length": 118.0,
        "width": 72.0,
        "height": 29.0
      },
      "corner_radius_mm": 18.0,
      "display": {
        "face": "front",
        "x_pct": 38.0,
        "y_pct": 42.0
      },
      "display_window_mm": {
        "width": 34.0,
        "height": 20.0
      },
      "intake": {
        "face": "front",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 78.0
      },
      "usb": {
        "face": "right",
        "x_pct": 50.0,
        "y_pct": 50.0
      },
      "cmf": {
        "material": "ABS",
        "finish": "textured_light",
        "color": "Dark graphite grey, NCS S 7500-N equivalent, moulded-in pigment (no paint), L* ~ 34",
        "secondary_ops": [
          "pad_print"
        ]
      },
      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the pebble silhouette: plan-view corner radii >= 15 mm on all four corners and a continuous convex radius around the full top edge, so no sharp corner can chip or catch on a desk edge.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Keep the front face as a single uninterrupted field: display window and intake grille are the only openings, both flush; do not add trim rings, bezels, logos, buttons or secondary apertures that raise part count or tooling cost.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Keep textured_light finish on both shell halves in moulded-in dark grey ABS; no paint, no soft-touch, no gloss. This is the scuff- and fingerprint-hiding surface and it must not be sanded or polished out downstream.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Keep the parting line as a single low horizontal seam below the front-face centreline, with a 0.8 mm step-free shadow gap; this one straight line is the only visible split and must stay straight and continuous around the part.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Keep the intake as a low horizontal slot grille (max 3 slots) moulded directly into the front shell, placed in the lower third so it is shielded when the unit is knocked over; no separate grille part or mesh.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA6",
          "statement": "Keep the display window small (<= 36 x 22 mm) and recessed 0.5 mm, using a flat lens bonded into the shell rather than a separate bezel assembly; the window area is the only non-textured gloss element and must remain a minority of the front face.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA7",
          "statement": "Keep wall thickness at 2.0 mm nominal with no ribbing in the shell halves; the pebble radius and low mass (<= 180 g) are what let the housing absorb desk-height knocks without a separate impact structure.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The direction asks for a soft pebble and the contract asks for the cheapest possible tidy box, so the concept spends its budget on radius rather than on parts. A pebble plan-form with 18 mm corner radii is free at the tool: it is the same two-cavity mould as a hard rectangle but removes the sharp corners that chip and the stress risers that crack on a 0.75 m desk drop, which is the contract's durability requirement met with geometry instead of material. Keeping the slab low (29 mm) and the footprint under 120 x 72 mm respects the 125 x 75 x 30 envelope and leaves the 180 g mass ceiling comfortable with ~92 g of internals. The front face is deliberately empty: one small display window at 38/42 percent and a three-slot intake grille in the lower third are the only features, so there is exactly one lens, no bezel, no buttons, no light pipe, and a single printed logo. That keeps the part count at two mouldings plus a lens and a label, which is what the CNY 12 ceiling needs; the relaxation headroom above the CNY 9.36 floor absorbs tooling amortisation rather than added features. Moulded-in dark graphite ABS in textured_light is the cheapest finger- and scuff-hiding surface available: no paint line, no soft-touch cure, no colour matching between halves, and the light grain scatters scratches so desk wear reads as texture rather than damage. The low straight parting line is the one piece of visual discipline that keeps the object from looking like a cheap shell, and the USB on the right face keeps the front field clean so the product still reads as tidy at retail."
    },
